# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in values for YOUR OWN dev/staging project.
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are read by the app, and every one of them is
# bundled into the client and readable by anyone with the app. Never put a
# service-role key, database password, OAuth client secret, Apple key,
# Resend API key or payment-gateway secret here.

# --- Public client configuration (required) -------------------------------
# Supabase project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Supabase anon / publishable key (NOT the service_role / secret key).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- Sign-in providers and e-mail: NOTHING goes in this file ---------------
# Google, Apple and verification e-mails (Resend SMTP) are configured on the
# server side only. The app asks Supabase which providers are enabled
# (GET /auth/v1/settings) and shows "not configured yet" for the others.
#   Google OAuth client ID + secret  -> Supabase Dashboard > Authentication > Providers > Google
#   Apple Services ID, Team ID, Key  -> Supabase Dashboard > Authentication > Providers > Apple
#   Resend API key (SMTP password)   -> Supabase Dashboard > Authentication > SMTP Settings
# Names and placeholders: supabase/server-secrets.env.example
# Step-by-step setup and verification: docs/v1/AUTH_PROVIDER_SETUP.md
